From 4f280d14843c3a0b51761c7f781fc9602968fa00 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pdale-boop <237306950+pdale-boop@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 00:42:56 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Characters and scenery: Wind Waker HD's light buffer, its
 point and effect lights on their light

Characters: Wind Waker HD's point and effect lights on its character light

Wind Waker HD sends the game's point lights (torches, lamps, lanterns) and effect lights (bombs, chests, the
sword-hit flash, the thunder) to a light buffer: each light adds colour x sat(N.L) x sat(1 - d / r)^1.5 into a
half-size buffer, and the characters' toon shader adds 1.75 times it to the light after the ramp mix, with no shadow,
cloud or ramp (read from Cemu: a lamp at Windfall at 21:00 takes Link's hair in the shade from 0.02 to 0.41 in red).
Under HD's character light the lights didn't reach the characters at all.

DOL_AURORA_POINT_LIGHTS_HD=1 (read once, off unless set): the host sends the lights on HD's rule
(aurora_set_point_lights: radius 2.3 x power for a point light, the power for an effect light, colour S10 / 255 with
no clamp), and the draws with HD's character light sum them per pixel at their own view-space position and normal,
the same sum as HD's buffer without its upsample. The frame's lights go to the camera's view space once, in
begin_actor_light_pass, into a uniform at group 0 binding 7 (gxc::HdPointLights, up to 32); the off group has none.
The light cap goes from 16 to 32 (the torch light's loop too). The light is the characters' only while their HD light
is on and the torch light is on (the host sends lights only then).

gxcore tests: the WGSL has the lights at binding 7 and HD's falloff; the reference sum checks a lamp straight on, at
45 degrees and out of reach; Link's hair under the Windfall lamp comes out (0.410, 0.382, 0.002) against HD's stored
(0.4105, 0.3831, 0.0043), the rim the rest. The flagged modules compile with Dawn (Vulkan, core and compatibility).
The pipeline cache version goes to 16.

Scenery: Wind Waker HD's point and effect lights on the lit scenery's light

Wind Waker HD's terrain and room shaders add its light buffer (the point and effect lights, the same sum the
characters take) to the light, outside the vertex colour and before the albedo multiplies it: (vertex colour x light +
1.25 x the buffer) x albedo (Cemu: Windfall's terrain at 21:00, Dragon Roost Cavern's and the Tower of the Gods'
rooms). In BlueWake the torches and lamps lit the scenery only through the torch glow added over the frame.

With DOL_AURORA_POINT_LIGHTS_HD=1 and HD's character light on, a draw whose TEV stage 0 is the GameCube's light,
lerp(C0, KONST, RASC) from colour channel 0 with no later stage reading C0 (gxc::hd_point_light_stage(): the field
terrain, the palms, and 16 of 18 and 25 of 26 of the two dungeons' room materials; no toon draw), takes a flagged
shader (ShaderKey::hd_point_light). It adds HD's sum x 1.25 to stage 0's result in linear light, so the stages
after it multiply the texture by it, as HD does. Its lights are the characters' (group 0 binding 7 of the actor
light group, which a flagged pipeline takes too); the off group has none and leaves the draw as before. The position
is the view-space one. The normal is the smooth one the sun shadows make for the scenery (in the vertices' normal
slot, turned by the position matrix as the sea mask's pass turns it; HD's own normals where the importer wrote
them), else the draw's own where its vertex shader works one out (a lit channel with a vertex normal), else the
triangle's from the position's screen derivatives, turned to the camera (indoors, where the sun shadows are off).

Left as they were: the channel is 8-bit as the TEV's inputs are, so a lamp lights a surface up to its texture's own
colour, not past it as HD can; the sun shadows' shade, applied after the scene, takes the added light in shade with
the rest; HD's SSAO (applied after the scene, on the shade) isn't on the term; the toon draws with HD's SSAO (the King
of Red Lions' 1.75 x AO) aren't matched.

gxcore tests: the classifier takes the pattern and refuses a later C0, another stage 0 and colour channel 1; the
flagged module has the lights, the position after the texcoords, the triangle's normal before any branch and the sum
on stage 0's light before stage 1; with a lit channel and a vertex normal it takes that normal, and with the smooth
normals the normal slot. The flagged modules
compile with Dawn (Vulkan, core and compatibility). The pipeline cache version goes to 17.

The sun shadows' shade no longer darkens the lamps' light: HD adds 1.25 x AO x P
after its shade, so the shade pass (fs_sun_map) takes the light buffer too and
multiplies the scene by (lit x shade + 1.25 x P x AO) / (lit + 1.25 x P), HD's
sunlight standing in for the vertex light. That also gives the lamps' light HD's
AO where the sun is. Not on the sea or characters. The sun map's uniform grows
by the light list (100 -> 360 floats).

Characters and scenery: no effect-light stage and no torch glow under Wind Waker HD's light buffer

Two stopgaps stood in for Wind Waker HD's light buffer while it wasn't ported: the GameCube's effect-light stage on
HD's character light (PREV + K1 x the ramp: the sword-hit flash, bombs, the item get), and the torch glow added over
the frame (the point lights' falloff squared x 0.35, three times their radius, no N.L). With the buffer on, the same
lights reach the characters and the lit scenery in their own draws, so each stopgap counted them twice.

While HD's light buffer is drawn (post_fx::point_lights_hd_active(), and the characters took HD's light this frame),
the effect-light stage is left out (HdActorLightConstants screen.z 0), as HD's toon shader has no such term, and the
torch glow isn't drawn. With the buffer off both stay as they were. DOL_AURORA_ACTOR_LIGHT_HD_EFFECT=1 or 0 keeps or
leaves out the stage either way, to compare.

Checked in BlueWake, Linux, Vulkan: Windfall at 21:00 and Dragon Roost Cavern's first room, against the build before
the light buffer. gxcore tests pass; the changed modules compile with Dawn.
